sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-015: Candidate Recommendations for Team Leads — Recommendation Sequence
    actor TeamLead
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant RecommendationService as Recommendation<br/>Service
    participant AvailabilityPool
    participant PostgreSQL

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Find compatible candidates for an open slot
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/teams/:teamId/slots/:slotId/recommendations
    ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART, and team ownership
    alt Unauthorized, non-owner, or invalid identifiers
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, or 403 with explicit code
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Keep vacancy context and offer Retry
    else Authorized owner
        ExpressAPI->>RecommendationService: Recommend for teamId and slotId without eventId
        RecommendationService->>PostgreSQL: Load team, open vacancy, and Confirmed members by requesting team_id
        PostgreSQL-->>RecommendationService: Team, slot, and requesting-team member set
        RecommendationService->>AvailabilityPool: Read platform-wide active LFT candidates
        AvailabilityPool->>PostgreSQL: Query fixed internal availability-pool row and permitted profiles
        PostgreSQL-->>AvailabilityPool: Active candidate cards
        AvailabilityPool-->>RecommendationService: Platform candidate pool
        RecommendationService->>RecommendationService: Revalidate active verified PART, not suspended, LFT on, not owner, not on requesting team
        alt No eligible candidates
            RecommendationService-->>ExpressAPI: Empty result with exclusion summary
        else Eligible candidates
            RecommendationService->>RecommendationService: Score skills plus role, goal, and hours from 0 to 100
            alt Scoring runtime fails
                RecommendationService-->>ExpressAPI: Degraded unranked eligible list and notice
            else Scoring succeeds
                RecommendationService->>RecommendationService: Sort by score, display handle, then internal tie key
                RecommendationService-->>ExpressAPI: Ranked cards and human-readable contributions
            end
        end
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Sanitized recommendation response
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Ranked, empty, degraded, or retryable state
        TeamLead->>ReactUI: Invite selected candidate
        ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/teams/:teamId/invitations
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: US-017 success or eligibility/quota failure
    end

    Note over RecommendationService,PostgreSQL: The normal path excludes Confirmed members by requesting team_id and ignores shadow-event lifecycle. A legacy event-scoped fallback remains if that membership query fails.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: Current recommendation cards expose participantId for invitation wiring even though the current story calls for no internal identifiers in the client response.

